+
+## Resize-independent coordinates
+
+New pose sidecars store canonical and native image x/y positions as normalized fractions of image width and height, clamped to `[0, 1]` (`coordinates.schema: 2`, `unit: "normalized"`). Bounding-box corners are also clamped; confidence, depth in its native units, embeddings and physical pose values are preserved. MediaPipe depth retains its native normalized units. `image_size` records original inference dimensions.
+
+`read_pose_result` resolves positions for the current image by default; use `as_pixels=False` for stored fractions. `draw_pose` accepts either representation. Resizing is supported; crop/rotation/orientation changes need a separate transform.
+
+Preview existing sidecar migration with `mp normalize-coordinates /photos`, then apply with `--write`. Readers and migration also support schema 1 `unit: "percent"` records by dividing by 100 and clamping. This conversion needs no image dimensions. Migration repairs out-of-range normalized records and is idempotent. Legacy pixel records without original dimensions are skipped; supply `--source-size WIDTH HEIGHT` only when those original dimensions are known. Migration retains model versions/timestamps and other namespaces, including `face.*`.
